  "stem": "In the \\(xy\\)-plane, the graph of \\(y = 3(x - 2)^{2} + k\\), where \\(k\\) is a constant, passes through the point \\((4, 5)\\). What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-7"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Substitute \\(x = 4\\) and \\(y = 5\\): \\(5 = 3(4 - 2)^{2} + k\\).",
    "\\(3(2)^{2} = 12\\), so \\(5 = 12 + k\\) and \\(k = -7\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x, k = symbols('x k')\nsol = solve(Eq(3*(4 - 2)**2 + k, 5), k)\nassert sol == [-7]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [-7]",
